<Project>

  <!-- Exists for exactly one reason, and goes away with the submodule.

       Viewer, AndroidViewer and WebLlvm reach Khalkos3D transitively, through Khalkos3dBridge, and
       the engine's projects live in external/Khalkos3D — so they are NOT in CupriFace.slnx. When
       MSBuild builds a solution it resolves every ProjectReference against the solution's
       configuration table, and the default for a reference with no entry in that table is to
       DISCARD the parent's Configuration rather than inherit it. The reference then falls back to
       the referenced project's own default, which is Debug.

       `dotnet build CupriFace.slnx -c Release` was therefore copying the DEBUG-built engine into
       the Release output of all three apps: correct file names, correct sizes, no warning, no
       error — just unoptimised code and a JIT told not to optimise it either. Setting this to
       false makes an unmapped reference inherit the parent's Configuration instead.

       THREE THINGS WORTH KNOWING, because each one cost a build to find out:

       It has to be here, on the CONSUMERS. Putting it on Khalkos3dBridge does nothing: the bridge's
       own output was always correct, because ProjectReference is transitive and it is each app that
       resolves the engine for itself.

       Per-reference SetConfiguration metadata does not work — AssignProjectConfiguration overwrites
       it from the solution table.

       Building a .csproj directly always resolved correctly, and naming a project file is all CI
       ever does, so CI was green throughout and would have stayed green. This only ever bit a local
       or IDE build of the solution, which is also the build anyone would profile. -->

  <PropertyGroup>
    <ShouldUnsetParentConfigurationAndPlatform>false</ShouldUnsetParentConfigurationAndPlatform>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <!-- There is no Directory.Build.props at the repo root today. If one is ever added, this import
       is what stops it being silently ignored for everything under samples/, because MSBuild stops
       walking up at the first one it finds. Resolved into a property first: a Condition cannot
       contain the nested single quotes the property function needs. -->
  <PropertyGroup>
    <_ParentBuildProps>$([MSBuild]::GetPathOfFileAbove('Directory.Build.props', '$(MSBuildThisFileDirectory)../'))</_ParentBuildProps>
  </PropertyGroup>
  <Import Project="$(_ParentBuildProps)" Condition="'$(_ParentBuildProps)' != ''" />

</Project>
